th>7</Month><Day>4</Day><Hour>5</Hour><Minute>0</Minute></PubMedPubDate><PubMedPubDate PubStatus="pmc-release"><Year>2003</Year><Month>7</Month><Day>1</Day></PubMedPubDate></History><PublicationStatus>ppublish</PublicationStatus><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">12839783</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC165208</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1128/AEM.69.7.4067-4075.2003</ArticleId></ArticleIdList><ReferenceList><Reference><Citation><b>Alef, K., P. Nannipieri, and C. Trazer-Cepedo.</b> 1995. &#x3b2;-Glucosidases, p. 325-344. <i>In</i> K. Alef and P. Nannipieri (ed.), Methods in applied soil microbiology and biochemistry. Academic Press, London, United Kingdom.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation><b>Banfield, J. F., and R. J. Hamers.</b> 1997. Processes at minerals and surfaces with relevance to microorganisms and prebiotic synthesis, p. 81-122. <i>In</i> J. F. Banfield and K. H. Nealson (ed.), Geomicrobiology: interactions between microbes and minerals. Mineralogical Society of America, Washington, D.C.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation><b>Banfield, J. F., B. F. Jones, and D. R. Veblen.</b> 1991. An AEM-TEM study of weathering and diagenesis, Abert Lake, Oregon. I. Weathering reactions in the volcanics. Geochim. Cosmochim. Acta 55<b>:</b>2781-2793.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation><b>Bensen, D. R., and W. B. Silvester.</b> 1993. Biology of <i>Frankia</i> strains, actinomycete symbionts of actinorhizal plants. Microbiol. Rev. 57<b>:</b>293-319.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC372911</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">8336669</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation><b>Brinch-Iversen, J., and G. M. King.</b> 1990. Effects of substrate concentration, growth state, and oxygen availability on relationships among bacterial carbon, nitrogen and phospholipid phosphorous content. FEMS Microbiol. Ecol. 74<b>:</b>345-355.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation><b>Burleigh, S. H., and J. O